messages:
Ravi K: quick sync: customers keep tripping on fetch in different runtimes. do we have a unified SDK approach?
Monica H: short answer: prefer globalThis.fetch when present, fallback to undici via dynamic import in Node, and document polyfills.
Ethan Z: agree. important: undici v5 is ESM-only, so bundling it accidentally into edge builds breaks. dynamic import helps but bundlers sometimes still inline it.
Ravi K: typing + TS pain: many users don't enable DOM lib so `fetch` type is missing. we should export a FetchLike type and show tsconfig snippets.
Monica H: example minimal adapter I want to land:
```js
export async function resolveFetch() {
  if (typeof globalThis.fetch === 'function') return globalThis.fetch;
  try {
    // try require for CJS consumers
    // eslint-disable-next-line global-require
    const und = require('undici');
    if (und && typeof und.fetch === 'function') return und.fetch;
  } catch (e) {}
  try {
    const mod = await import('undici');
    if (mod && typeof mod.fetch === 'function') return mod.fetch;
  } catch (err) {
    throw new Error("@redwood/inference: no Fetch implementation found. Install undici for Node <18 or provide a global fetch polyfill. See docs: https://docs.redwood.ai/sdk/fetch");
  }
}
```
Ethan Z: docs should include a quickstart matrix: Node <18 (install undici + polyfill snippet), Node 18+ (no-op), Bun (note quirks), Deno/Edge (global fetch).
Ravi K: onboarding note: show entrypoint polyfill for CJS apps: `(async ()=>{ globalThis.fetch = (await import('undici')).fetch; })();` and for ESM `globalThis.fetch = (await import('undici')).fetch;`.
Monica H: TS guidance: recommend "lib": ["ES2020","DOM"] in tsconfig or add `/// <reference lib="dom" />` in files. also export `export type FetchLike = typeof fetch;` as fallback.
Ethan Z: publishing note: do NOT put undici in dependencies. leave it as an opt-in install to avoid surprising edge bundling. add bundle-check CI to assert undici not present in edge example builds.
Docs Bot: opened doc draft: /sdk/fetch-guidance with polyfill snippets, tsconfig examples, and troubleshooting FAQ entry.
Ravi K: decision: implement runtime-detect adapter, dynamic import require-try, clear error message, docs + examples. action owners: Monica -> adapter + tests, Ethan -> CI bundle checks + perf job, Ravi -> docs review and onboarding blurb.
